# resq secrets allowlist
#
# GitHub Actions workflow files contain pinned commit SHAs in `uses:` directives
# (40-char hex strings). The secrets scanner flags these as high-entropy secrets,
# but they are SHA pins — a security best practice, not leaked credentials.
#
# The scanner only supports literal file-path exclusions, not pattern-based or
# line-level ignores. These entries are scoped to workflow YAML only; all other
# files remain fully scanned.
#
# If actual secrets are added to workflow files, they should use ${{ secrets.* }}
# references (which don't embed the secret value) — never literal values.
.github/workflows/auto-merge.yml
.github/workflows/chromatic.yml
.github/workflows/ci.yml
.github/workflows/labeler.yml
.github/workflows/label-sync.yml
.github/workflows/octoguide.yml
.github/workflows/post-release.yml
.github/workflows/pr-review-requested.yml
.github/workflows/pr-size-labeler.yml
.github/workflows/release-package.yml
.github/workflows/release.yml
.github/workflows/security.yml
.github/actions/prepare/action.yml
